From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alan Bradburne <abradburne@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 20:01:42 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: rk3568: make the WDT and TSADC trigger a first
 global reset

The RK3568's watchdog and thermal sensor trigger a second global reset
by default, which leaves the SoC hung instead of restarting it: an
expired watchdog never brings the board back. On the RG DS+ a slot on
trial whose init never started systemd stayed hung for over ten minutes
with SPL's watchdog running, and a reboot that needed the watchdog hung
with only a backlight on. Set both to a first global reset in SPL, as
PX30 does.

Upstream status: proposed on the U-Boot list in June 2026 ("rockchip:
rk3568: make the WDT trigger a first global reset", and the TSADC
patch); not merged in v2026.10. Drop this when it is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3568/rk3568.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3568/rk3568.c b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3568/rk3568.c
index 0a6607e5..43c69948 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3568/rk3568.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3568/rk3568.c
@@ -28,6 +28,10 @@
 
 #define PMU_BASE_ADDR		0xfdd90000
 #define PMUCRU_BASE_ADDR	0xfdd00000
+#define CRU_BASE_ADDR		0xfdd20000
+#define CRU_GLB_RST_CON		(0xdc)
+#define GLB_RST_CON_TSADC_FIRST	BIT(0)
+#define GLB_RST_CON_WDT_FIRST	BIT(1)
 #define PMUCRU_PMUGATE_CON0	(0x180)
 #define CLK_RTC32K_FRAC_GATE	BIT(1)
 #define PMU_NOC_AUTO_CON0	(0x70)
@@ -157,6 +161,15 @@ int arch_cpu_init(void)
 	 * which s2idle and suspend use, never completes.
 	 */
 	writel(CLK_RTC32K_FRAC_GATE << 16, PMUCRU_BASE_ADDR + PMUCRU_PMUGATE_CON0);
+
+	/*
+	 * Make the watchdog and the TSADC trigger a first global reset, as
+	 * on PX30. The default, a second global reset, leaves the SoC hung
+	 * rather than restarting it: a watchdog that expires never brings
+	 * the board back, and a thermal shutdown doesn't either.
+	 */
+	setbits_le32(CRU_BASE_ADDR + CRU_GLB_RST_CON,
+		     GLB_RST_CON_WDT_FIRST | GLB_RST_CON_TSADC_FIRST);
 #endif
 	return 0;
 }
